		body: [
			`SEO tools like Ahrefs and SEMrush are staples in <a href="/blog/what-digital-marketing-is-what-it-is-not/">digital marketing</a>, but leaning on them too heavily can be misleading, since their traffic estimates are often best-guess approximations. A page might show 200 monthly visitors in Ahrefs while Google Search Console shows it's actually pulling in over 5,000.`,
			`<h3>The Long-Tail Opportunity Everyone Misses</h3>`,
			"About 70% of keywords are long-tail, and these popular tools tend to underrepresent them in favor of the short and medium-tail keywords everyone is already competing for. The smartest approach focuses on the long-tail terms competitors overlook, since they often carry high conversion intent even at low search volume.",
			`<h3>Where the Real Search Opportunity Is</h3>`,
			`The best organic search results tend to come from strategies rooted in real customer conversations: using Google auto-suggest, related searches, and low- or zero-volume keywords to find the exact language buyers use at the point they're ready to act. Working as an <a href="/services/fractional-ai-advisor/">AI marketing consultant</a>, I find these underrepresented long-tail terms consistently outperform the high-competition keywords tools push you toward. This approach fits within a <a href="/blog/digital-marketing-strategies-tips-best-practices/">broader digital marketing strategy</a> built around actual buyer behavior rather than tool outputs.`,
		],
